# ns4-OrganPreset — read coverage over the specimen sweep. Runs of bits sharing a verdict.
#
# varies   an instrument writes this bit two ways (OR against AND over every
#          corpus specimen of this body; all-ones bodies excluded). ⚠️ The
#          committed fixtures are left out of this column: they are this
#          crate's own writers' output over a zeroed body, so their unclaimed
#          bits are evidence of nothing.
# claimed  the path declaring it, from the layout — intent, not a read. A path
#          marked (unregistered) is declared but reports no value.
# answers  registry paths whose value moved when the bit was flipped and the
#          file re-parsed, over the sampled specimens; `refused` is the parser
#          rejecting the mutated file, which is a read too.
#
# Offsets are body-relative — a hex dump of the file adds the container's body
# start, 0x2c on a type-1 header and 0x18 on a type-0. Bits inside a byte are
# numbered LSB-first: `0x51[3:2]`.
#
# 1112 bits; varies over 64 corpus specimens, answers over 3 flipped.

bits           at                                 claimed by                                   varies  verdict    answers
0..=40         0x00..0x05+0x05[7]                 —                                            no      spare      —
